# Without this file, `docker compose build` sends the entire repo — including every local `bin/`/`obj/`
# directory from whatever machine ran a `dotnet build`/`dotnet test` outside the container — as the build
# context. The Dockerfile's own `COPY src/ src/` then overwrites the container's freshly-restored (Linux)
# `obj/` output with those host `obj/` files, which bake in host-specific paths (e.g. a Windows machine's
# NuGet fallback folder under `C:\Program Files (x86)\...`). `dotnet publish --no-restore` then fails inside
# the container trying to resolve a Windows path that doesn't exist on Linux. Found by actually running
# `docker compose up --build` for the first time — see PROJECT_STATUS.md.
**/bin/
**/obj/
.vs/
.vscode/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
node_modules/
*.user
logs/
